      "html": "<p>This loach belongs to the family of river loaches (Balitoridae). It is a peaceful species that is suitable for a well-kept aquarium. The final length should not exceed 6 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_beavani_wrong_determined_s_scaturigina__en/",
      "html": "<p>It originates from Darjeeling and Assam in the eastern Himalayan mountains, Northern India, Nepal and Bhutan.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_beavani_wrong_determined_s_scaturigina__en/",
      "html": "<p>It lives in fast streaming rivers.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_beavani_wrong_determined_s_scaturigina__en/",
      "html": "<p>This loach should be kept in a well filtered and aerated fish tank with water having a high oxygen content.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/schistura_beavani_wrong_determined_s_scaturigina__en/",
      "html": "<p>They are omnivorous with a preference for mosquito larvae.</p>"
